# FloodLens-X Development Rules

## Scope
Work only on the task explicitly requested.
Do not perform speculative refactors or unrelated cleanup.

## Token efficiency
Use the smallest sufficient solution.
Read only files relevant to the task.
Reuse existing code before creating new code.
Do not duplicate existing functionality.

## Dependencies
Do not install new dependencies unless necessary.
Prefer the existing project stack.

## Architecture
Respect existing module boundaries.
Do not rewrite working architecture without explicit approval.

## Numerical core
Treat validated numerical components as protected.
Do not change numerical equations, algorithms, solver behavior,
or validated numerical constants unless explicitly requested.

## File scope
Modify only files necessary for the current task.
Avoid large rewrites when a targeted change is sufficient.

## Testing
Run the smallest relevant test suite after changes.
Never claim success without verification.

## Safety
Do not delete or overwrite unrelated work.
Do not modify files outside the requested scope.

## Completion
Stop when the requested task is complete.
Do not add optional features unless requested.

## Final response
Report:
- files changed
- what was implemented
- tests run
- remaining issues
